    "rationale": "Final design. I accepted the round-2 critique's main point that kd is risky, and partly accepted its point about ki. I kept the other changes from the revision.\n\nEvidence: no tested design has finished or stayed on the line. Every design (iterations 0 and 1) left the line at max_error of about 0.061 m, just past the 0.06 m off-track limit. Progress was 0.035 to 0.115 on the s-bend and slalom and 0.12 to 0.18 on the oval. Steering oscillation was low (0.06 to 0.14). Both the effective gain of 5 and the effective gain of 1.5 failed in the same way, so gain alone is not the main cause. The early failure on the s-bend and slalom points to the start or the first bend, not to jitter.\n\nChanges from the revision:\n1) kd 0.2 to 0.0. The critique is right that kd on sensor-edge steps dominates the proportional term, and the evidence shows little oscillation for kd to damp. Setting kd to 0 also isolates the proportional and integral changes in this race.\n2) ki 1.0 to 0.5. The critique is right that ki 1.0 is not sized and could drift, since the accumulation rate is unknown. I still want enough integral action to remove the fixed motor mismatch, so I chose a middle value. Its contribution is bounded by the integral cap of plus or minus 2 (at most 1 turn unit at ki 0.5).\n\nKept:\n- kp 2.0 and the weights [-1,-0.5,0,0.5,1]. The critique's gain-authority concern is valid, but the evidence does not show that gain is the cause, so I did not change it again.\n- base_speed 1.2. base_pwm is 4095 x 0.6 = 2457, leaving about 1638 counts of headroom, so clipping is not a concern. Completion is not expected at this speed, and the 500-point completion term is accepted as lost.\n- wheel_track 0.14, mass 0.8, body and wheel geometry, sensor layout (y 0.05, 16 mm spacing, 12 mm footprints), and line_loss last_direction.\n\nRejected: I did not change the start behaviour in this revision, because changing it together with the gains would again confound the result. The full measurement request is kept so that max_error timing and line_loss_events can show whether the failure is at the start or at a bend.\n\nExpected (hypothesis, not observed): max_error below 0.055 m, line_loss_events at most 1, and higher progress on the s-bend and slalom than 0.04. Completion is not expected.\n\nDecision rule for the next iteration: if max_error is still about 0.061 with the same timing of line loss, the cause is the start, so the next design should change initial alignment and line_loss handling. If rms_error rises while steering_oscillation stays low, raise ki. If steering_oscillation rises, lower kp first.",
